cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DataDiver or its findings, please cite it."
title: "DataDiver: a real-time intelligence surface for San Francisco and Oakland civic data"
abstract: >-
  DataDiver is a civic-data visualization platform that turns public open
  data from San Francisco (data.sfgov.org) and Oakland (data.oaklandca.gov)
  into map- and chart-based views designed to surface anomalies, trends, and
  patterns for journalists, researchers, and residents. Software is licensed
  MIT; editorial content and original derived datasets are licensed CC BY 4.0.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jesse
    family-names: Garnier
    affiliation: "San Francisco State University, Department of Journalism"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sfbay/datadiver"
url: "https://datadiver.jlabsf.org"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - civic data
  - open data
  - data journalism
  - data visualization
  - San Francisco
  - Oakland
